From f6ca733d61b9518e6ce298080dcf1868338ba5a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: StachowiakDawid <dawidos234@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 18:38:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ipa: softisp: contrast detection autofocus with a lens on the
 simple pipeline

The simple pipeline handler with the software ISP has no autofocus and
never drives a focus lens. Add the pieces for a contrast detection AF:

- SwStatsCpu adds a focus measure to SwIspStats: the sum of the squared
  differences between horizontally adjacent luminance samples (one per
  4 pixels, the samples the statistics already take) in the middle half of
  the image in both directions, with the sum and number of samples. Cost:
  one subtraction and multiplication per sample in a quarter of the image.
- The IPA configuration gets the lens controls, and a new setLensControls
  event carries V4L2_CID_FOCUS_ABSOLUTE back; the simple pipeline handler
  passes the focus lens of the sensor (CameraSensor::focusLens(), from the
  lens-focus ancillary link) and applies the event with
  CameraLens::setFocusPosition(), like the IPU3 pipeline does.
- A softisp "Af" algorithm: coarse scan over the lens range, fine scan
  around the peak, parabolic interpolation of the peak, final approach
  from below; AfMode Manual/Auto/Continuous,
  AfTrigger Start/Cancel, AfState metadata. The starting AfMode comes from
  the tuning file (default manual). Without a lens the controls are removed.

The measure is divided by the squared mean luminance so the AGC can keep
running during a scan. LensPosition is not offered: there is no dioptre
calibration of the lens positions.
